From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:18:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a stack give its last element the room left

A text at the end of a vertical stack (a game's description under its
name, data and facts) starts wherever the elements above it end, so
no fixed height suits it: the stack cut it in the middle of a line at
its bottom. A vertical stackpanel with fillLast gives its last shown
element the room left under the others, and a text with maxLines in a
box of a height of its own keeps no more lines than the box holds
whole, the last one ending with an ellipsis.
